GenoMining Section 3: Data Preprocessing and Exploratory Analysis

Start with README.md. It contains the introduction, an example, setup commands, file descriptions, data flow, findings and study guidance for this branch.

Quick start after installing requirements.txt:
  python -m section3.run
  python -m section3.build_notebook --execute

Folder map:
  section3/          Focused analysis, executed notebook, study notes and submission helpers.
  section3/outputs/  Four figures, evidence tables, matrices, transformers and audits.
  section3/reports/  PDF and editable Markdown reference report.
  readmission/       Shared data loading and preprocessing components.
  data/              Public source data and patient-separated cohort, generated locally.
  tests/             Focused integrity tests in test_section3.py.

Example use: inspect prior inpatient-visit distributions and prepare a 147-column numerical matrix from 20 selected inputs. The README explains how to load that matrix and its matching row ledger.

The final academic report is written and verified by the team. The supplied reference and study guide help explain the executed work.
